## Code facts confirmed

- MuseFileName schema refuses any approval file name that is not a plain name, and refuses "." and "..".
- Approval row ids must equal a picture-list row id before they are used; the writer never forms a path from a row id.
- Delivery copy targets come only from the picture-list row names, which the file-name pattern pins.
- All structural checks run before the first write; manifest.json is written last.
- A different existing manifest is refused; an existing delivery file with different bytes is refused (color and line).
- SHA-256 values come from the byte buffers that the writer copies.
- The writer maps only a Kimi review and a named person review; a model evidence class on a person review is refused by schema.
- The writer reads local files only: no fetch, no child process, no env read, no credential.
- The deliver CLI errors pass the redactSecrets boundary of scripts/storytime-book-pictures.ts.

## Findings

- RB8-01 Major: deliver pins no picture-list SHA-256. (code reading; confirmed)
- RB8-02 Major: --delivery and --muse accept paths outside out/ and outside the repository. (code reading; confirmed)
- RB8-03 Nit: writes are not exclusive creates; a dangling symlink at a delivery target receives the delivered bytes. (code reading; probe blocked by tool permission)
- RB8-04 Nit: duplicate picture-list names within one run can overwrite an earlier copy silently. (code reading; probe blocked by tool permission)
- RB8-05 Nit: degenerate line-art list names "." and "manifest.json" pass the plain-name check. (code reading; probe blocked by tool permission)
- RB8-06 Nit: Muse reads follow symlinks out of museRoot. (code reading; probe blocked by tool permission)
- RB8-07 Nit: T152 to T161 cover no path or validation refusal. (code reading; confirmed)

## Probe status

The sandbox denied probe scripts: writes under /tmp, heredocs, and tsx -e programs containing dynamic import were refused by tool permission. RB8-03 to RB8-05 rest on code reading only. The working probe pattern for a later session is a short static-import tsx -e program that imports /home/daniebo/Desktop/advantage-forge/src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts.

